{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `obs_t_calib`, `obs_t_fall`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: the elementwise `obs_t_fall[n, h] ~ normal(...)` likelihood inside nested loops was replaced by a single vectorized sampling statement on the top-level protected variable `obs_t_fall`. In `data_safe.json`, `obs_t_fall` is the deterministic flattening of the original `N_drops` by `N_heights` array in the same nested-loop order: `(n = 1, h = 1:N_heights)`, then `(n = 2, h = 1:N_heights)`, and so on. The model computes the corresponding mean vector after all parameter priors and before the observation statement. The calibration observations `obs_t_calib` are represented as a vector with the same values. These changes preserve the original product normal likelihood while satisfying SafeStan's requirement that protected data be observed exactly once with a plain top-level sampling statement.
","model_safe_stan":"functions {
  real t_fall(real g, real h, real v0) {
    return (v0 + sqrt(square(v0) + 2 * g * h)) / g;
  }
}

data {
  // Detector calibration data
  int N_calibrations;
  vector[N_calibrations] obs_t_calib;    // seconds

  // Falling data
  int N_heights;
  array[N_heights] real<lower=0> heights;    // meters
  int N_drops;
  vector[N_drops * N_heights] obs_t_fall; // seconds, flattened by drop then height
}

parameters {
  real<lower=0> sigma_t; // seconds
  array[N_drops] real v0;      // meters per second
  real<lower=0> sigma_v; // meters per second
  real g;                // meters per second squared
}

model {
  vector[N_drops * N_heights] mu_t_fall;

  // Prior model
  sigma_t ~ normal(0, 0.5);
  sigma_v ~ normal(0, 1);
  v0 ~ normal(0, sigma_v);
  g ~ inv_gamma(1.49, 2.83);

  // Observational model
  obs_t_calib ~ normal(rep_vector(0, N_calibrations), sigma_t);

  for (n in 1:N_drops) {
    for (h in 1:N_heights) {
      mu_t_fall[(n - 1) * N_heights + h] = t_fall(g, heights[h], v0[n]);
    }
  }
  obs_t_fall ~ normal(mu_t_fall, sigma_t);
}

// Simulate a full observation from each value of the parameters
generated quantities {
  array[N_drops, N_heights] real obs_t_fall_post_pred;

  for (n in 1:N_drops) {
    for (h in 1:N_heights) {
      real mu_t_fall = t_fall(g, heights[h], v0[n]);
      obs_t_fall_post_pred[n, h] = normal_rng(mu_t_fall, sigma_t);
    }
  }
}
","data_safe_json":"{"N_calibrations":5,"N_drops":2,"N_heights":5,"heights":[1.9430348025241297,1.967220948563611,2.8738898073965613,1.2162956482120266,2.1753293121890733],"obs_t_calib":[5.568798001347895,2.9203628787442137,6.79269848961036,5.874516337490485,6.128843056129548],"obs_t_fall":[6.289786128324222,4.583501718882629,6.079435047190338,2.637886644238364,5.4860768956460255,4.217756921810382,4.7188961085555565,4.474723345994659,4.794394518451915,2.2548735327028]}","protected_variables":["obs_t_calib","obs_t_fall"]}
